  "body": "Currently I'd have to do `sp.toString() && '?'+sp`\r\n\r\nideally, .toString() would behave similarly to `URL#search`, so like this: \r\n```js\r\nvar sp = new URLSearchParams('');\r\nsp+'' == '' // like now\r\n\r\nvar sp = new URLSearchParams('?x');\r\nsp+'' == '?x=' // with a leading ?\r\n\r\nvar sp = new URLSearchParams('?');\r\nsp+'' == '' // like now\r\n```\r\nbut it's too late\r\n\r\nShould it be a new method?",
